     1	# V025 — design freeze and closure rule (controller, 2026-09-09 ≈ 02:45 UTC; sealed before any formal successor outcome)
     2	
     3	The review loop has no stopping condition as it stands: each round of outside opinion or fresh-context audit produces amendments, which produce another round. This rule closes it.
     4	
     5	## 1. Freeze point
     6	The successor design is **frozen when engine stage 4g passes its audit**. From that moment the sealed set is: declarations v1.0–v1.9 and their errata, the contingency ladder and its amendment, the stages 6–8 contract v1 with amendments v1.1–v1.2, and every controller decision record in force. No further scientific change is made before the a-r0 matrix.
     7	
     8	## 2. Admissibility test for a late finding (all four must hold)
     9	A finding arriving after the freeze is acted on **only if**:
    10	1. it can change the **sign** of a load-bearing certificate or the **branch** of the admission trichotomy — stated in one sentence, with which certificate;
    11	2. it names a **test that fails now and passes after the change**, executable in under an hour;
    12	3. it is confirmed by a source independent of the one that raised it (a second reviewer, or a measurement);
    13	4. the change does not require re-running work already completed under the freeze, or, if it does, the re-run fits in one overnight window.
    14	A finding that fails any of the four is recorded in `LIMITATIONS-AND-FUTURE-WORK-REGISTER.md` with its reasoning and is reported in the paper's limitations section. This is not a way to hide problems: the register is published with the work.
    15	
    16	## 3. What continues after the freeze
    17	Outside opinions and audits continue, because their findings still shape the **limitations, the claim wording and the next study** — but they no longer gate the matrix. Engineering fixes that change no scientific quantity (speed, memory, logging, reporting fields) remain allowed at any time and are listed in the stage reports.
    18	
    19	## 4. Standard of evidence for calling something a defect
    20	Every item recorded as a defect carries: the failing test or the changed number, the independent confirmation, and what it would have done to a certificate. An item with none of these is labelled **precautionary**, not a defect, and is not used to justify delay. The register `V025-DEFECT-REGISTER-2026-09-09.md` applies this standard retrospectively to everything acted on so far, so that the owner can audit which changes were demonstrated and which were precautionary.
    21	
    22	## 5. Deadline discipline
    23	If stage 4g's audit does not return READY within two further engine passes, the controller stops adding scope, runs the matrix on the last audited configuration, and reports every unresolved item in the register as a declared limitation.
     1	# V025 priority declaration — v1.6 amendment (controller; sealed 2026-09-09 ≈ 01:20 UTC, before any formal successor outcome)
     2	
     3	v1.0–v1.5 are preserved unchanged. This amendment applies the round-8 outside opinion (`OUTSIDE-ROUND8-CHATGPT-QA-2026-09-09.md`). **Disclosure: these changes followed inspection of development SMOKE numbers** (the a-r0 vertical slice and the regime slice on a quarantined world). No value below was chosen to make any observed number better; each is fixed by the declared channel model, by an accounting identity, or by a convention stated with its rationale. The primary architecture, arms, δ, QoS margins, panel and seeds are unchanged. Every item applies **identically to every arm** (carrier BASE proposal, U1/J1 ceilings, S0, S_UNI, FULL and all DROP arms).
     4	
     5	## 1. Selection-time scoring uses a declared fading margin (remedy for the nominal-vs-realised gap)
     6	Selection scores are computed on margin-adjusted channel gains: for every link, ĥ_margin = ĥ_nominal · q₁₀, where q₁₀ is the **10th-percentile quantile of the declared keyed fading distribution** (shadow + scintillation) at that link's actual elevation, evaluated from the sealed channel model in closed form (no new telemetry, no realised draw). The score is internally consistent: F_m(a) = B_m(a) − η_ref·E_m(a) − Φ(a) with service, ACM mode, required power, bits and energy all recomputed under ĥ_margin. Rationale for the 10 % level: the standard 90 %-availability link-budget convention; it is not fitted to any outcome. Diagnostic only (never decision-bearing): the same anchors rescored at q₀₅ and q₂₅ with the top-1 agreement rate. KAT: with the fading distribution collapsed to a point mass, margin scoring is bit-identical to nominal scoring. **Executed physics, labels, the committed profile's evaluation and the endpoint remain unchanged at 48 boundaries with realised fading.**
     7	
     8	## 2. C2 enters the set-level selector as a tie-break only
     9	The set-level continuation term ranks only among the maximisers of the immediate margin-adjusted score (deterministic tie-break; ties defined by a declared 1e-9 relative tolerance). Q2's separate role in forming the per-user proposal a⁰ is unchanged. Before the formal matrix, the engine reports the three-way diagnostic that separates an implementation defect from forecast error from a genuine trade-off: (a) at matched anchors, ΔI_N ≤ 0 and ΔI_N + Σ_h Δc_h^N ≥ 0 for the immediate-optimal vs continuation-optimal profiles; (b) per offset, the split of (ΔF_realised,48 − ΔF_nominal,snapshot) into an integration error and a fading error; (c) the **joint future continuation minus the sum of singleton future continuations** (the round-8 suspect: immediate C3 corrects only the current interaction, so summed per-move continuations can stay optimistic at every future offset). The diagnostic is reported, not gated.
    10	
    11	## 3. Coordination is measured by net collision avoidance, and Ψ is additionally re-anchored
    12	At matched anchors, with D(a) = Σᵢ dᵢ(a), a_D = the additive-selection profile and a_C = the interaction-aware profile (identical anchors, catalogue, margin and C2 rule): report V_CA = [F(a_C) − F(a_D)]/κ together with both components (interaction loss avoided, singleton value sacrificed), unclipped, plus the frequency of reversals where D(a_D) > 0 and D(a_D) + Ψ(a_D) < 0. Additionally, the decomposition is reported **twice**: anchored at the carrier a⁰ (as now) and **re-anchored at the certified S_UNI local optimum u**, where dᵢ^u ≤ 0 by construction, so any improving joint escape must have Ψ_A^u > 0. The slice's negative Σg_I measures interaction loss *incurred* around the carrier and is not evidence against coordination. The operational certificate remains realised pooled EE against certified S_UNI; V_CA is a mechanism certificate.
    13	
    14	## 4. Admission certificates: load-bearing vs informative, and a pre-declared trichotomy
    15	Load-bearing for the a-r0 admission decision: (i) S0's **realised** pooled-EE gain reported beside its nominal prediction; (ii) S0 vs **certified** S_UNI (matched information, objective, budget and fallback accounting; termination certificate present, else the comparator is labelled budget-limited and the contrast is not load-bearing); (iii) the corrected factor-oracle marginals under the final C2 rule; (iv) realised availability/QoS, physics validity and deadline behaviour with timeout/fallback outcomes counted in B and E. Informative but not decisive: J1 − U_all (two purely additive good moves can exceed the best single move). Diagnostics only: cap-hit, plateau share, ACM distribution, lit beams.

